.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH bhtune-history-list 1  "bhtune-history-list " 
.SH NAME
bhtune\-history\-list \- List past runs, newest first
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbhtune\-history\-list\fR [\fB\-\-outcome\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-offset\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List past runs, newest first
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-outcome\fR \fI<OUTCOME>\fR

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
running
.IP \(bu 2
completed
.IP \(bu 2
failed
.IP \(bu 2
aborted
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR [default: 50]

.TP
\fB\-\-offset\fR \fI<OFFSET>\fR [default: 0]

.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: table]
How to print the run list
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Human\-readable text (default)
.IP \(bu 2
json: Pretty\-printed JSON. This is the external contract for scripted/scheduled consumers, so its shape must not change silently once shipped
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
